# Every cinematic of the game loads after the VR overlays (#495): the owner's headset run crashed in the AMD driver
# inside glTexImage2D while akbaa_dream_c.cin loaded its images, right after the menu pointer's beam had been
# created. The beam, the reticle rings and the desktop mirror's overlays set GL_UNPACK_ALIGNMENT to 4 and left it;
# the engine's images are tightly packed, so the next RGB tile whose row is not a multiple of 4 (akbaa dream.tga's
# last column, 110 x 256: 330-byte rows read 332 apart) was read 510 bytes past its buffer. GLTexture::upload now
# sets the tight state itself and logs an [E] with the numbers when the state it found is not the engine's tight
# one - so this sequence creates the beam first and then loads all 19 .cin of data.pak (every image uploaded on
# load, --cinematics so a development launch shows them), skipping each with B as a player would: no [E], errors 0.
# With the leak put back (the three glPixelStorei lines) the first upload after the beam reports it and the run
# is red: proven once on 2026-10-17, PR #505.
#
# Runs on the test save mvp-items (#70: controls free, a key on the table, the bag closed):
#   .\scripts\dev\xrs-run.ps1 cinematics
# (smoke-test.ps1 -Sequence takes the arx.exe arguments from its own command line, TRAPS.md: with it pass
#  -VrSim idle -Save mvp-items -- --loadslot 0 --cinematics)
@sim idle
@save mvp-items
@args --loadslot 0 --cinematics

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false

# The menu pointer's beam (#34): the bag open on the floating panel, the right hand aiming at the key - the beam
# image is uploaded (RGBA 8 x 64), the pixel-store state the cinematic tiles meet next
inventory playeraddfromscene key_base_0005
@frames 5
ui inventory open
@until vr.panel.mode eq world 5s
@frames 60                                   # the bag slides up
vr-sim head rot 0 -20 0
@frames 5
vr-point right item
@frames 5
@assert vr.pointer.active eq true
@assert vr.pointer.beam eq true
@log VRSystem:.*menu pointer: beam image
ui inventory close
@until vr.panel.mode eq head 5s
@frames 5

# Each cinematic: the script command prepares it, the next frame loads it (every image cut into 256 x 256 tiles and
# uploaded) and starts it; the right B skips it (#394) and the game is back in gameplay
cine akbaa_dream_a
@until state eq CINEMATIC 60s
@log CinematicLoad:.*Loading cinematic "graph/interface/illustrations/akbaa_dream_a\.cin"
vr-input tap right.b
@until state eq GAMEPLAY 30s
@frames 5

cine akbaa_dream_b
@until state eq CINEMATIC 60s
@log CinematicLoad:.*Loading cinematic "graph/interface/illustrations/akbaa_dream_b\.cin"
vr-input tap right.b
@until state eq GAMEPLAY 30s
@frames 5

# The owner's crash: akbaa dream.tga 1390 x 1390, the last column of tiles 110 wide
cine akbaa_dream_c
@until state eq CINEMATIC 60s
@log CinematicLoad:.*Loading cinematic "graph/interface/illustrations/akbaa_dream_c\.cin"
@assert errors eq 0
vr-input tap right.b
@until state eq GAMEPLAY 30s
@frames 5

cine end_game
@until state eq CINEMATIC 60s
@log CinematicLoad:.*Loading cinematic "graph/interface/illustrations/end_game\.cin"
vr-input tap right.b
@until state eq GAMEPLAY 30s
@frames 5

cine end_game_new
@until state eq CINEMATIC 60s
@log CinematicLoad:.*Loading cinematic "graph/interface/illustrations/end_game_new\.cin"
vr-input tap right.b
@until state eq GAMEPLAY 30s
@frames 5

cine end_game_old
@until state eq CINEMATIC 60s
@log CinematicLoad:.*Loading cinematic "graph/interface/illustrations/end_game_old\.cin"
vr-input tap right.b
@until state eq GAMEPLAY 30s
@frames 5

